Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:18:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] docs(process): weight every issue by effort and route it
 to a matching worker agent

AGENTS.md Issue Law gains "Every issue is weighted by effort": one
effort:low|medium|high|max label beside P*, set at filing from a table,
with a safety floor (G-code, collision, sim, geometry and every P0 are at
least effort:high). Issues are dispatched to .claude/agents/issue-worker-
<effort>.md (haiku / sonnet / opus / fable), which run the new shared
/work-issue skill. Reviews run at least on the medium tier (high under the
floor). A worker that fails its gate twice or finds the work bigger
escalates the label one step and releases the issue. The review-prs cost
comment records the effort and any escalation for recalibration.

PROCESS_VERSION 5 -> 6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
